== MUTATION TESTS ON THE RE-POINTED PROBES, 23 September 2026
==
== WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Eleven probes went green the first time they were
== re-pointed at the door the product funds through. A suite that has only
== ever been seen green is a suite nobody has watched fail, and on this
== project a probe has already reported PASS over a door that could not
== insert a row. So each mutation below breaks ONE thing on purpose, in an
== ISOLATED COPY of the migrations and the script under /tmp, and the run is
== kept. Nothing here touched the repository's own migrations or the live
== project.
==
== MUTATION A: public.escrow_fund_proposal_as inserts a column that does not
==   exist, which is the exact shape of the 09:32 fault on 23 September.
== MUTATION B: public.escrow_propose_as inserts a column that does not exist,
==   so the OPENING half of the door cannot make a row.
== MUTATION C: public.escrow_fund_proposal_as stops refusing an amount the
==   payer cannot afford (`if spendable < e.amount_minor` becomes `if false`).
==   The smoke check passes, because one uncontested funding call of an
==   affordable amount is still fine. The contention probes are what must
==   notice.

